      "writtenOn": "2026-05-11T21:09:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks like it has the potential to hit some asserts as well? The default `utils::SystemHandle` constructor called above if the handle is -1 is created with a value of `kInvalidHandle` (OS specific). The `SharedFence` mostly uses the handle without checks, but in `SharedFence::DestroyImpl()` it calls `mHandle.Close()`, which asserts that the handle `IsValid()`.\n\nSee https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/utils/SystemHandle.cpp;l\u003d165;drc\u003dc83b80f441edc1c50de8d3977fa3feeb0ae96bc3\n\nProbably just need to check for `mHandle.IsValid()` in `SharedFence::DestroyImpl()` before attempting to close it.",
      "revId": "cd04b5b03a54e97bf218497107f4410022f4aa1b",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
